                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_15\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit changes FileHandler.java's fileMatcher visitFile method from:\n    String tempPath = fileName.toString();\nto:\n    String tempPath = location.relativize(path).toString();\nThis restores the relative path (directory + filename) instead of just the bare filename, fixing a bug where the spec/config dropdown only showed the filename.\n\nTracing the history of this exact line across the candidates:\n- candidate_04 introduced fileMatcher() originally using `path.toString().replaceAll(location + \"/\", \"\")`, i.e. computing a relative path manually \u2014 this preserved subdirectory information.\n- candidates_07/10/11/12/13/14 only tweaked case-folding, camelCase conversion, and separator handling, but always kept the relative-path-derived value (still based on `path`, not just the filename).\n- candidate_15 is the commit that refactored fileMatcher to change its signature to take a Path `location`, switched the match target from `path` to `path.getFileName()`, and set `tempPath = fileName.toString()`. This is precisely the regression: it discarded the relative directory portion and kept only the bare filename, matching the described bug (\"only showed the filename without suffix\" being lost in the surrounding relative path context).\n- candidate_16 is the actual fix commit itself, changing `fileName.toString()` back to `location.relativize(path).toString()`.\n\nSince candidate_15 is the first (and only) commit that introduces the `tempPath = fileName.toString()` line that the fix directly reverts, it is the bug-introducing commit.\n"
                }
